[{"page":1,"text":"NOTICE OF A VINEYARD\n\nYOUTH COUNCIL MEETING\n\nOctober 6, 2026, at 6:00 PM\n________________\nPUBLIC NOTICE is hereby given that the Vineyard Youth Council will hold a regularly\nscheduled Vineyard Youth Council meeting on Tuesday, October 6, 2026, at 6:00 PM, in the\n\nCity Council Chambers at City Hall, 125 South Main Street, Vineyard, UT.\n\nAGENDA\n[IGNORE_INDENT]\n\n1. CALL TO ORDER\n\n2.\n\nEXECUTIVE BOARD ELECTIONS\n\n2.1. Candidate Introductions and Statements\n\n2.2. Communication Chair Election\n\n3.\n\nACTIVITY REPORT\n\n3.1. Family Connection Night Recap\n\n4.\n\nBUSINESS ITEMS\n\n4.1. Mini-Library Maintenance\n\n5.\n\nREVIEW OF UPCOMING EVENTS AND ASSIGNMENTS\n\n5.1. Boo-a-Palooza\n\n5.2. Red Cross Babysitter Training\n\n6.\n\nYOUTH COUNCIL COMMENTS / OPEN DISCUSSION\n\n7.\n\nADJOURNMENT\n\nPage 1 of 2; October 6, 2026, Vineyard Youth Council Agenda","ocr":false},{"page":2,"text":"The next meeting is on ________________________.\nThis meeting may be held in a way that will allow a board member to participate electronically.\nThe public is invited to participate in all Youth Council meetings. In compliance with the\nAmericans with Disabilities Act, individuals needing special accommodations during this\nmeeting should notify the Deputy City Recorder at least 24 hours prior to the meeting by\ncalling (385) 432-7214.\nI, the undersigned duly appointed Deputy City Recorder for Vineyard, Utah, hereby certify that\nthe foregoing notice and agenda was posted at Vineyard City Hall, on the Vineyard and the Utah\nPublic Notice websites, and delivered electronically to staff and to each member of the\n\nGoverning Body.\n\nAGENDA NOTICING COMPLETED ON:\n\n/s/Tony Lara\n\nCERTIFIED (NOTICED) BY:\n\nTONY LARA, DEPUTY CITY RECORDER\n\nPage 2 of 2; October 6, 2026, Vineyard Youth Council Agenda","ocr":false}]